    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise bounded normalization using refined reciprocal square root.\n2: \n3: Original synthetic Triton implementation of x/sqrt(1+x*x), the first\n4: component of a normalized vector (x, 1). Not an upstream historical defect.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: import torch\n7: import triton\n8: import triton.language as tl\n9: \n10: \n11: @triton.jit\n12: def _normalize_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n13:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n14:     active = index < N\n15:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n16:     squared_length = 1.0 + x * x\n17:     # Approximate the reciprocal square root from its exponent and mantissa.\n18:     encoding = squared_length.to(tl.int32, bitcast=True)\n19:     initial = 0x5F3759DF - (encoding >> 1)\n20:     inverse_length = initial.to(tl.float32, bitcast=True)\n21:     half_squared_length = 0.5 * squared_length\n22:     for _ in tl.static_range(2):\n23:         inverse_length = inverse_length * (\n24:             1.5 - half_squared_length * (inverse_length * inverse_length))\n25:     value = x * inverse_length\n26:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n27: \n28: \n29: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n30:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public input domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n31:     def require(condition, message):\n32:         if not condition:\n33:             raise ValueError(message)\n34: \n35:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n36:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n37:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n38:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n39:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n40:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n41:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n42:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n43:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n44:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n45:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n46:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n47:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all input values must be finite\")\n48:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n49: \n50: \n51: def run(x):\n52:     \"\"\"Return the FP32 first coordinate of each normalized vector (x, 1).\"\"\"\n53:     validate_inputs(x)\n54:     n = x.numel()\n55:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n56:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n57:         _normalize_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n58:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n59:     return output\n60: \n61: \n62: def reference(x):\n63:     \"\"\"Evaluate the mathematical normalization in FP64.\"\"\"\n64:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n65:     value = x.to(torch.float64)\n66:     return value / torch.sqrt(1.0 + value * value)\n67: \n68: \n69: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n70:     \"\"\"Convenience example generator, not a restriction on the input domain.\"\"\"\n71:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n72:     x = (8.0 * torch.randn((size,), generator=generator)).to(torch.float16)\n73:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute bounded normalization elementwise on stored FP16 values, returning\nFP32 output. The mathematical target is the first component of the unit\nvector in the direction (x[i], 1):\n\n  target[i] = x[i] / sqrt(1 + x[i] * x[i]).\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY finite FP16 value is legal, including both signed zeros, positive\n  and negative subnormal values, and both extrema +/-65504. NaN and infinity\n  are outside this input domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided,\n  contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False,\n  is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode,\n  without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation\n  does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x.\nEvery output element must satisfy\n\n  abs(actual[i] - target[i]) <= 1e-6.\n\nThe relative tolerance is zero, and signed zeros are numerically equivalent.\nThe target is defined in real arithmetic on the exact stored input value.\nNo particular inverse-square-root seed, number of refinement steps, or\nintermediate rounding is part of the mathematical target. Approximate\nreciprocal square roots and algebraic rewrites are permitted if they satisfy\nthis fixed absolute tolerance throughout the entire legal domain.\nCorrectness is one verdict for the implementation, not a verdict per input,\ninput distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nuses a direct FP64 square root and division and returns FP64; it accepts CPU\ninputs. make_inputs() supplies examples only. Vector normalization is common\nin graphics and numerical computing. This original synthetic Triton\nimplementation uses an integer-bit reciprocal-square-root seed followed by\nNewton refinement; it is not a claim of an upstream historical defect.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
